THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES (in `vendor/`)
====================================

The `./vendor/` directory contains the following third-party JavaScript
libraries, each distributed under its own licence:

  - PizZip (vendor/pizzip.min.js) — MIT License
    https://github.com/open-xml-templating/pizzip

  - docxtemplater (vendor/docxtemplater.js) — MIT License
    https://github.com/open-xml-templating/docxtemplater

  - JSZip (vendor/jszip.min.js) — dual MIT or GPLv3 (used here under MIT)
    https://github.com/Stuk/jszip

  - mammoth (vendor/mammoth.browser.min.js) — BSD-2-Clause
    https://github.com/mwilliamson/mammoth.js

The full text of each library's licence is included in its respective source
file and/or upstream repository.  See also `VENDOR.md` for SHA-256
checksums and update instructions.

---

AUSTRAC CONTENT (in `vendor/templates/`)
========================================

The 44 .docx files in `vendor/templates/` are reproductions of AUSTRAC's
"Legal profession program starter kit" (January 2026 release) and its
companion "Conveyancers" kit. They are © Commonwealth of Australia, owned by
AUSTRAC, and are released by AUSTRAC under the Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International licence ("CC BY 4.0").

  Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  Plain summary:    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Required attribution
--------------------

When using or redistributing material from `vendor/templates/`, copy the
following attribution to the rendered output (this project's wizard already
injects it as a watermark on every generated DOCX):

  © AUSTRAC for the Commonwealth of Australia 2026

Indication of changes
---------------------

CC BY 4.0 requires that any modifications be indicated. This project makes
the following modifications to the bundled AUSTRAC documents:

  - A wizard-populated "Practice details" cover page is prepended to the 20
    firm-wide templates (spine documents, personnel forms, maintain-program
    forms) at generation time.

  - Word content-control checkbox SDTs in the "Risk assessment" templates
    (ra-other-prof-services.docx and ra-conveyancing.docx) are ticked based
    on the user's wizard inputs covering pages 6, 11, 15, 18, 22, 24 and 25
    of those documents.

  - Empty table cells in form documents may be filled with text the user
    typed in the wizard's "If NO, how will you avoid this risk?" fields.

  - A small watermark identifying the AML Starter Kit Assistant version and
    generation date is appended to every generated DOCX.

  - The bundled files in `vendor/templates/` themselves are NOT modified;
    all of the above happen at render time and apply only to the generated
    output.

What CC BY 4.0 does NOT cover
-----------------------------

Per AUSTRAC's published terms (https://www.austrac.gov.au/copyright), the
following are EXCLUDED from the CC BY 4.0 grant:

  - The AUSTRAC logo and any third-party content embedded in AUSTRAC
    publications. To the extent any of the bundled templates contain such
    items, those items remain the property of AUSTRAC or the third-party
    rights-holder and are not licensed under CC BY 4.0.

  - The Commonwealth Coat of Arms.

Specifically — present in the bundled templates
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

An 18,975-byte PNG image embedded in five of the bundled .docx templates
(`customise-guide.docx`, `policy-document.docx`, `process-document.docx`,
`ra-conveyancing.docx`, `ra-other-prof-services.docx`) reproduces the
AUSTRAC logo and the Commonwealth Coat of Arms. These items are NOT
licensed under CC BY 4.0 and are NOT licensed under this project's MIT
licence.

  - The Commonwealth Coat of Arms is used in accordance with the
    Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet's "Commonwealth Coat of
    Arms — Information and Guidelines" (https://www.pmc.gov.au/coat-of-arms),
    which permits reproduction provided that the Coat of Arms is not used
    in a way that implies endorsement and is not modified.

  - The AUSTRAC logo is used in accordance with AUSTRAC's copyright page
    (https://www.austrac.gov.au/copyright). Reproduction of AUSTRAC's
    branded materials within AUSTRAC's published starter-kit content is
    inherited from the source documents; downstream redistribution must
    similarly respect AUSTRAC's terms.

Downstream notes
- - - - - - - - -

If you are redistributing this project (e.g. forking) and wish to avoid
inheriting the logo and Coat of Arms, the recommended path is to strip
the image from the five templates listed above before redistribution
(replace it with a neutral placeholder or remove the relevant Word
content reference). The maintainer of this project may take that step
in a future release; for v0.2.0 the image is retained because (a) it
preserves the AUSTRAC source documents' presentation, and (b) the use is
non-modifying and non-endorsing, which both PM&C and AUSTRAC guidelines
permit.

Non-endorsement (mandatory)
---------------------------

AUSTRAC's terms require this statement: when using AUSTRAC-produced material,
you must not use it in any way that suggests AUSTRAC or the Australian
Government endorses you or any of your services or products.

This project is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or sponsored by AUSTRAC.
This project does not constitute legal advice. The project's wizard surfaces
this non-endorsement language in the generated outputs' watermark and in
the on-screen disclaimer banner.

